    "id": "ldpc-quality-compatible-alist-v1",
    "issue": "c077a88b",
    "purpose": "decoder-family",
    "description": "Confirmatory comparison of screen-selected quality-compatible LDPC decoder cells: the gf2-coding f32 flooding normalized-min-sum decoder against the AFF3CT v4.7.0 configurations shortlisted by the bounded capability screen, on bit-identical parity-check matrices and bit-identical recorded LLRs. Precision, schedule and native SIMD wave size differ between the arms and stay labelled; the timed batch size is identical. It estimates comparator gaps under frozen decision margins and makes no adoption decision. Each call includes decoder construction, conversion, output and destruction. The identical timed batch is processed by both arms; latency is per batch, and throughput is frames per batch divided by batch time. Prepared 128-frame quality evidence is reused without resampling. Warm timing uses fixed fixture bank zero: the first recorded frame for matched latency and the first sixteen recorded frames for quality-compatible batch throughput. The remaining recorded frames supply quality validation, not additional timed samples. Both arms load the same recorded AList and construct their native sparse matrix and decoder inside each call; no encoder is initialized. This is recorded-AList operation version 1; prior fixture-constructor attempts are excluded from this family's resolution evidence. Exact upstream revisions, actual compiler/backend observations and executable identities are pinned by dev/bench_results/c077a88b/2026-09-08-r4-c077a88b-preparation/build-identity.json (SHA-256 e2c2c9f2a8e10f1e7a98d7b48ea2c6079515cf30f0d60f48f73377fcb9d64f30). The receipt snapshots this record and the complete producing-input closure. Confirmation excludes the pilot cells dvb-t2-r12-i16-inter-pilot under their predeclared quality rule; their measurements and P-19 findings remain in the cited pilot receipt."
  },
  "frozen": {
    "frozen_utc": "2026-09-08T12:19:30.410407+00:00"
  },
  "effect": {
    "worthwhile_speedup": null,
    "rationale": "This family reports a comparator gap and adopts nothing, so it declares no worthwhile speedup; the material-gap threshold below is the margin it decides on.",
    "measurement_resolution": 0.02,
    "resolution_evidence": {
      "receipt": "dev/bench_results/c077a88b/2026-09-08-r4-c077a88b-ldpc-quality-compatible-pilot/receipt.json",
      "sha256": "647cecd904866c9be0598c72325e8d2732fd36b4f8756e2c49ef4549e50987ec"
    },
    "equivalence_margin": 1.04,
    "equivalence_rationale": "Twice the pilot-observed measurement resolution of 0.020. A comparator within that factor of the gf2 decoder is not a gap this host can resolve, so the family declares it equivalent rather than reading a difference the harness cannot see.",
    "material_gap_threshold": 1.08,
    "material_gap_rationale": "Four times the pilot-observed measurement resolution of 0.020, and outside the equivalence margin. A comparator faster than that on a whole-consumer decode is a gap a consumer would notice on a real frame budget and one that needs an attributed explanation rather than a note."
  },
